### 🔹 1. Kaplan-Meier Model (KM)
```r
library(survival)
# KM model - overall survival
km_fit <- survfit(Surv(futime_years, status) ~ 1, data = df)
summary(km_fit, times = 5)  # Get 5-year survival probability
```
---

### 🔹 2. Cox Proportional Hazards Model (CoxPH)
```r
# Cox model with covariates (e.g., age, sex, bmi)
cox_model <- coxph(Surv(futime_years, status) ~ age + male + bmi + type, data = df_model)
summary(cox_model)
```
---

### 🔹 3. Parametric Survival Model (e.g., Weibull)
```r
# Using the flexsurv package
library(flexsurv)
weibull_model <- flexsurvreg(Surv(futime_years, status) ~ age + male + bmi + type, data = df_model, dist = "weibull")
summary(weibull_model)
```
---

### 🔹 4. Competing Risks Model (Fine-Gray)
```r
library(cmprsk)
# Assuming "status" = 1 for event of interest, 2 for competing risk
fg_model <- crr(ftime = df$time, fstatus = df$status, cov1 = df[, c("age", "male", "bmi", "type")])
summary(fg_model)
```
---

### 🔹 5. Accelerated Failure Time (AFT) Model
```r
aft_model <- survreg(Surv(futime_years, status) ~ age + male + bmi + type, data = df_model, dist = "weibull")
summary(aft_model)
```